# Git Commit Messages

## Subject line

- Imperative mood, capitalized, no trailing period
- Aim for 50 chars; hard limit 72
- Use `fix:` prefix for bug fixes, `revert:` for reverts; otherwise start with a verb (`Add`, `Fix`, `Update`, `Refactor`, `Remove`, `Enhance`, `Clean up`)
- Be specific — name the function, parameter, or feature

```
# Good
Add StartImportByAPI parameter to catalog feed job steps
fix: splitFile() header corruption and customer checkpoint on full export

# Bad
fixed stuff / Update README.md / changes
```

## Body (optional, encouraged for non-trivial changes)

- Blank line after subject; wrap at 72 chars
- Explain **why**, not what
- Prose for single issues; `-` bullets for multiple changes

## Footer

- `Fixes #n` / `Closes #n` / `Resolves #n` to auto-close GitHub issues
- `Co-authored-by: Name <email>` when applicable

## Avoid

- Vague subjects, present tense ("fixes", "adds"), trailing period
- `EXPBLD-XXX:` Jira prefix — historical only, no longer used
